WEBVTT

00:00:04.680 --> 00:00:07.400
I'll protect the three of them, indeed!

00:00:09.170 --> 00:00:10.450
Very well.

00:00:10.450 --> 00:00:14.780
I'll defeat you and become 
the leader of the Scoopers!

00:00:20.760 --> 00:00:21.980
Is that...

00:00:21.980 --> 00:00:23.190
The Amatsumara?

00:00:23.190 --> 00:00:25.880
Maybe Misa-chan's Amatsumara 
is responding to her.

00:00:26.080 --> 00:00:30.710
Impossible! How could an 
Amatsumara respond to a Scooper?

00:00:34.160 --> 00:00:36.040
You won't beat me, indeed!

00:02:10.950 --> 00:02:15.570
Misa-chan, the Amatsumara reacted 
to you because you're creative now.

00:02:16.020 --> 00:02:17.110
She's right.

00:02:17.110 --> 00:02:19.490
You made that ring out of beads.

00:02:19.750 --> 00:02:21.790
I'm creative?

00:02:22.330 --> 00:02:23.470
You are.

00:02:23.470 --> 00:02:26.380
You've been creative all along.

00:02:26.380 --> 00:02:30.460
In that case, we'll have to 
show the shrimp your power.

00:02:30.720 --> 00:02:31.290
Huh?

00:02:31.700 --> 00:02:34.130
Yes, indeed!

00:02:41.510 --> 00:02:43.080
Ow! Ow, ow, ow!

00:02:43.080 --> 00:02:44.350
What is this?!

00:02:51.350 --> 00:02:52.370
They're beads.

00:02:52.370 --> 00:02:56.230
I love beads, indeed!

00:02:56.230 --> 00:02:58.260
Misa-chan, that's amazing!

00:02:58.260 --> 00:03:01.020
But isn't this kind of a lot?

00:03:01.020 --> 00:03:03.550
It's better when there's more, indeed.

00:03:07.580 --> 00:03:09.440
This is nothing!

00:03:09.440 --> 00:03:12.540
You think you can accomplish 
anything with beads?

00:03:15.110 --> 00:03:15.750
Huh?

00:03:17.500 --> 00:03:19.720
Huh? Huh? Huh? Huh?

00:03:20.060 --> 00:03:22.220
Stop!

00:03:23.700 --> 00:03:25.020
Hurry, hurry!

00:03:25.020 --> 00:03:26.640
Uh-oh. He noticed.

00:03:26.640 --> 00:03:28.890
That was faster than I expected.

00:03:30.080 --> 00:03:31.350
Misa-chan?

00:03:31.940 --> 00:03:36.220
No matter what I do, 
I can only make beads, indeed.

00:03:36.220 --> 00:03:37.580
Misa-chan...

00:03:38.210 --> 00:03:42.850
You three were able to fully utilize the 
Amatsumara from the very start, indeed.

00:03:42.850 --> 00:03:45.350
Compared to you, I'm only...

00:03:45.350 --> 00:03:46.560
That's not true.

00:03:46.560 --> 00:03:48.020
You're amazing.

00:03:48.020 --> 00:03:50.700
You did something you 
thought you couldn't do.

00:03:50.700 --> 00:03:53.210
The rest should be easy.

00:03:53.670 --> 00:03:55.180
You can do it!

00:03:57.560 --> 00:03:59.590
Everyone...

00:04:00.960 --> 00:04:02.080
Hold it right there!

00:04:02.080 --> 00:04:03.930
Stop, stop, stop!

00:04:03.930 --> 00:04:05.910
We're not waiting for you!

00:04:05.910 --> 00:04:07.390
Let's run.

00:04:09.350 --> 00:04:10.960
This way!

00:04:15.250 --> 00:04:17.460
How to use the Amatsumara?

00:04:17.460 --> 00:04:19.640
How did we do it at first?

00:04:19.640 --> 00:04:26.910
The shrimp assigned us roles like offense, 
support, and dealing the finishing blow.

00:04:27.300 --> 00:04:31.620
Without really knowing what we were doing, 
we worked together to defeat the UFOs.

00:04:31.880 --> 00:04:34.440
Roles... Working together...

00:04:35.710 --> 00:04:36.780
Misa-chan.

00:04:37.820 --> 00:04:40.520
All these beads might work.

00:04:41.140 --> 00:04:43.800
Let's be creative together.

00:04:43.800 --> 00:04:44.880
Together?

00:04:45.210 --> 00:04:46.090
Yeah.

00:04:47.850 --> 00:04:51.020
Yes, indeed!

00:04:51.400 --> 00:04:54.580
If we use your Amatsumara, 
we can manage somehow.

00:04:55.040 --> 00:04:56.640
I'm sure we can beat the shrimp.

00:04:57.110 --> 00:05:00.540
But all I can make are beads.

00:05:01.030 --> 00:05:02.230
That's plenty.

00:05:02.700 --> 00:05:05.560
You made a ring out of beads,

00:05:05.560 --> 00:05:08.430
but there are plenty of other 
things you can make with beads.

00:05:08.430 --> 00:05:11.230
You can makes necklaces, 
brooches, and even bears.

00:05:11.230 --> 00:05:13.420
The possibilities are unlimited.

00:05:13.420 --> 00:05:15.390
Is that so, indeed?!

00:05:15.390 --> 00:05:18.310
So let's think of what we can 
make together and do our best.

00:05:18.310 --> 00:05:19.710
Yes, indeed.

00:05:19.970 --> 00:05:20.920
You're right.

00:05:20.920 --> 00:05:23.910
Making things together 
has always worked for us.

00:05:23.910 --> 00:05:26.520
Join us, Misa-chan!

00:05:28.280 --> 00:05:32.780
But... what should we make?

00:05:36.150 --> 00:05:41.860
Let's see... What can we make with beads 
that will be able to fight a giant shrimp?

00:05:42.340 --> 00:05:44.490
Since he's a shrimp, how about a cat?

00:05:44.860 --> 00:05:45.960
A cat?

00:05:45.960 --> 00:05:48.320
We'll turn the shrimp into cat food!

00:05:48.320 --> 00:05:49.950
Rito, a cat made of beads.

00:05:50.420 --> 00:05:52.660
Got it. A cat made of beads, right?

00:05:53.120 --> 00:05:55.500
I know how we can make it!

00:05:55.500 --> 00:05:58.500
If we build it by linking lots of hexagons,

00:05:58.500 --> 00:06:01.340
we'll be able to build it 
quickly, and it'll be strong.

00:06:01.340 --> 00:06:02.250
Got it.

00:06:02.250 --> 00:06:05.570
This structure was originally 
based on bee hives.

00:06:05.570 --> 00:06:08.710
These days it's even used in buildings.

00:06:08.710 --> 00:06:11.840
Oh, I want honey toast now...

00:06:11.840 --> 00:06:12.990
Sounds good.

00:06:12.990 --> 00:06:15.440
But we can eat once we're finished.

00:06:15.860 --> 00:06:17.370
Okay!

00:06:17.980 --> 00:06:21.690
You three really are amazing, indeed.

00:06:21.930 --> 00:06:23.060
It's done.

00:06:23.060 --> 00:06:23.770
Misa-chan.

00:06:24.200 --> 00:06:27.340
Think of a cute accessory 
we can put on this cat.

00:06:27.340 --> 00:06:28.940
Cute?

00:06:28.940 --> 00:06:31.120
Okay, indeed...

00:06:33.490 --> 00:06:36.200
A shiny star would be nice, indeed!

00:06:39.340 --> 00:06:40.010
How's this?

00:06:40.010 --> 00:06:41.100
It's nice.

00:06:41.100 --> 00:06:43.750
What will his name be?

00:06:44.250 --> 00:06:47.460
Super Beads Kitty, indeed!

00:06:47.860 --> 00:06:50.080
It's decided, then.

00:06:50.080 --> 00:06:52.430
Misa-chan, try praying to the Amatsumara.

00:06:52.850 --> 00:06:54.510
Got it, indeed!

00:07:00.470 --> 00:07:02.510
There's no point in hiding!

00:07:02.510 --> 00:07:03.480
Misa-chan!

00:07:03.480 --> 00:07:06.780
Right, indeed!

00:07:08.040 --> 00:07:09.120
Again?!

00:07:13.240 --> 00:07:14.260
Huh?

00:07:18.040 --> 00:07:20.000
Wh-What is this?

00:07:21.260 --> 00:07:23.760
Super Beads Kitty!

00:07:25.560 --> 00:07:26.640
Huh?

00:07:27.860 --> 00:07:29.240
Let's go!

00:07:29.240 --> 00:07:32.400
I won't be turned into cat food!

00:07:35.760 --> 00:07:36.390
That's it!

00:07:35.760 --> 00:07:38.100
Go!

00:07:36.390 --> 00:07:38.100
You can do it!

00:07:36.390 --> 00:07:38.100
Get him, indeed!

00:07:39.310 --> 00:07:41.040
Take this!

00:07:42.380 --> 00:07:43.330
Huh?

00:07:44.870 --> 00:07:46.190
Yeah!

00:07:46.190 --> 00:07:46.730
Huh?

00:07:49.370 --> 00:07:50.650
All right!

00:07:50.650 --> 00:07:52.030
You can do it, kitty!

00:07:52.030 --> 00:07:53.760
We did it, indeed!

00:07:53.760 --> 00:07:56.240
Keep beating the stuffing out of him!

00:07:57.430 --> 00:07:59.630
I-I was just testing you.

00:07:59.630 --> 00:08:03.310
I haven't shown you my true strength yet.

00:08:04.890 --> 00:08:07.380
This is my true strength!

00:08:09.030 --> 00:08:10.010
Huh?

00:08:12.960 --> 00:08:16.510
Since it's such an important attack, 
I'll use it twice—no, over and over again!

00:08:16.510 --> 00:08:18.350
Again, again, again!

00:08:18.840 --> 00:08:22.340
Wow, the kitty's dodging everything.

00:08:22.770 --> 00:08:25.310
Why don't you give up, shrimp?

00:08:28.580 --> 00:08:29.870
I see.

00:08:29.870 --> 00:08:32.530
Looks like I'll have to use my true strength.

00:08:33.020 --> 00:08:35.160
You said you were earlier.

00:08:35.160 --> 00:08:37.580
This is my actual true strength!

00:08:37.580 --> 00:08:38.640
Yeah, yeah.

00:08:38.640 --> 00:08:40.600
Take this!

00:08:40.600 --> 00:08:41.080
Yargh!

00:08:58.100 --> 00:08:59.380
Kitty!

00:08:59.900 --> 00:09:03.100
Hey, no one told us you could do that!

00:09:04.220 --> 00:09:07.040
Just like you eat a shrimp's tail last,

00:09:07.040 --> 00:09:10.360
you must also save your trump 
card until the very end!

00:09:15.020 --> 00:09:15.820
Kitty!

00:09:19.830 --> 00:09:22.210
Kotoko, is there anything we can do?

00:09:22.210 --> 00:09:24.380
If I predict the course of the boomerang...

00:09:24.380 --> 00:09:26.290
Oh, I can't calculate it in time!

00:09:26.600 --> 00:09:29.390
It would seem that this is the end.

00:09:29.390 --> 00:09:34.320
I'll finish you off by biting you in 
half with these sparkly white teeth!

00:09:36.570 --> 00:09:39.260
I win!

00:09:39.260 --> 00:09:41.140
You jump too high, shrimp.

00:09:41.140 --> 00:09:43.750
I'll calculate the strength of his 
joints from his range of movement.

00:09:43.750 --> 00:09:45.230
His weakness is...

00:09:45.230 --> 00:09:50.190
I couldn't be creative after all.

00:09:50.680 --> 00:09:52.840
Misa-chan, don't.

00:09:52.840 --> 00:09:57.040
Believe in the Super Beads Kitty that you made.

00:09:57.040 --> 00:09:58.160
Miss Rito...

00:09:58.160 --> 00:09:59.500
She's right.

00:09:59.500 --> 00:10:02.260
We made it together. He'll definitely win.

00:10:02.260 --> 00:10:02.870
Yeah.

00:10:04.120 --> 00:10:06.710
Yes... indeed.

00:10:07.040 --> 00:10:11.170
Super Beads Kitty, I believe in you!

00:10:18.610 --> 00:10:20.050
It revived itself!

00:10:20.050 --> 00:10:21.160
All right.

00:10:22.350 --> 00:10:24.340
No, you don't!

00:10:25.360 --> 00:10:26.620
I've got it!

00:10:26.620 --> 00:10:30.020
The joints in his jaw are structurally weak.

00:10:30.020 --> 00:10:30.650
Misa-chan.

00:10:30.650 --> 00:10:33.660
Kitty! Jump, indeed!

00:10:38.620 --> 00:10:39.840
Now, indeed!

00:10:39.840 --> 00:10:41.110
Go!

00:10:58.380 --> 00:11:01.220
Impressive, ladies.

00:11:01.530 --> 00:11:04.680
I'm amazed you've achieved this level 
of mastery over the Amatsumara.

00:11:04.680 --> 00:11:07.510
The Scoopers have evolved.

00:11:07.510 --> 00:11:11.620
There's no need for the 
Scoopers to steal anymore.

00:11:12.440 --> 00:11:13.440
We did it!

00:11:13.440 --> 00:11:14.460
We did it.

00:11:14.460 --> 00:11:16.840
Thanks to all of you, indeed.

00:11:17.310 --> 00:11:19.470
It's because we worked together.

00:11:19.470 --> 00:11:21.820
By the way, what should we do with that?

00:11:22.310 --> 00:11:26.220
I'm going to try talking to Ebifurya, indeed.

00:11:27.260 --> 00:11:30.650
I can't believe this happened.

00:11:31.200 --> 00:11:34.250
He's kind of cute when he's cowering.

00:11:34.250 --> 00:11:35.260
How?

00:11:35.260 --> 00:11:37.360
I take back what I said!

00:11:37.360 --> 00:11:40.070
Anyway, now that I'm relieved, I'm hungry.

00:11:40.070 --> 00:11:43.240
Maybe, but I'm not eating 
any more Scooper snacks.

00:11:43.240 --> 00:11:45.480
Let's make something ourselves, then.

00:11:53.200 --> 00:11:54.860
Now for the toppings.

00:11:55.290 --> 00:11:57.070
Where's the popping candy?

00:11:57.620 --> 00:12:00.220
Let's decorate it with lots of strawberries!

00:12:00.580 --> 00:12:03.030
Misa-chan, you try it.

00:12:05.490 --> 00:12:08.920
Cold, cold, cold, cold!

00:12:08.920 --> 00:12:10.480
It's like eating a shrimp live.

00:12:10.480 --> 00:12:13.620
A shrimp-flavored parfait is a novel idea!

00:12:13.620 --> 00:12:14.680
Yeah.

00:12:14.680 --> 00:12:16.880
Creating is fun, indeed!

00:12:19.900 --> 00:12:20.700
It's finished.

00:12:20.700 --> 00:12:22.320
That looks tasty, indeed!

00:12:22.320 --> 00:12:23.310
How wonderful.

00:12:23.310 --> 00:12:24.990
We did work hard on it.

00:12:24.990 --> 00:12:27.660
The ratio of whipped cream 
to ice cream is one to two.

00:12:27.660 --> 00:12:30.680
It's made so you'll experience all 
kinds of flavors as you keep eating.

00:12:30.680 --> 00:12:34.680
You're meant to add layers after calculating 
what texture you ultimately want,

00:12:34.680 --> 00:12:35.990
so its structure is...

00:12:35.990 --> 00:12:39.500
Kotoko, all the ice cream will melt 
if we wait until you're finished.

00:12:40.280 --> 00:12:42.360
This isn't a fantasy, is it?

00:12:42.360 --> 00:12:43.580
Of course not.

00:12:43.580 --> 00:12:47.490
It's our parfait that we made for ourselves.

00:12:47.490 --> 00:12:49.950
It's wonderful, indeed!

00:12:49.950 --> 00:12:52.340
Let's eat!

00:12:52.340 --> 00:12:54.040
It's delicious, indeed!

00:12:54.040 --> 00:12:55.210
Yeah.

00:12:55.210 --> 00:12:55.850
So good.

00:12:55.850 --> 00:12:56.910
It's so good.

00:12:56.910 --> 00:12:57.800
It's so cold!

00:12:57.800 --> 00:12:59.010
I'm so happy.

00:13:00.790 --> 00:13:01.800
Hey...

00:13:02.620 --> 00:13:04.630
Should we break that?

00:13:04.630 --> 00:13:05.260
That?

00:13:06.740 --> 00:13:07.840
Yeah.

00:13:07.840 --> 00:13:09.970
Are you sure?

00:13:10.380 --> 00:13:13.750
It's fun to make new things together.

00:13:13.750 --> 00:13:16.060
Yeah. Let's rebuild it from scratch.

00:13:16.060 --> 00:13:17.610
Both Harajuku and the parfait.

00:13:17.610 --> 00:13:19.330
I'm so excited!

00:13:19.330 --> 00:13:22.440
Let's go after we finish this.

00:13:31.060 --> 00:13:32.120
Here we go!

00:13:32.120 --> 00:13:33.450
Ready, go!

00:13:34.660 --> 00:13:36.670
Ready, go!

00:13:36.900 --> 00:13:38.560
Ready, go!

00:13:44.560 --> 00:13:45.420
Look.

00:14:11.320 --> 00:14:13.830
It's accessorizing with 
cherry blossom leaves.

00:14:13.830 --> 00:14:15.360
What a wonderful cat.

00:14:15.360 --> 00:14:16.670
Wait a minute.

00:14:16.670 --> 00:14:19.210
There aren't any cherry blossoms 
blooming here right now.

00:14:19.450 --> 00:14:22.760
What are you talking about? 
The cherry blossoms have always been...

00:14:22.760 --> 00:14:26.780
Oh, right. That was in our 
fantasy. We made it up.

00:14:26.780 --> 00:14:29.870
That's right. The cherry 
blossoms were our fantasy.

00:14:29.870 --> 00:14:31.040
That's why they disappeared.

00:14:31.040 --> 00:14:32.910
But this kitty hasn't.

00:14:32.910 --> 00:14:35.470
If we imagined it, it would've disappeared.

00:14:35.470 --> 00:14:36.620
You're right.

00:14:36.620 --> 00:14:38.060
What does that mean?

00:14:38.640 --> 00:14:43.270
This cat was inside the bubble
the whole time, just like us.

00:14:47.230 --> 00:14:48.780
How cute, indeed.

00:14:51.470 --> 00:14:52.930
Want some fish sausage?

00:14:52.930 --> 00:14:54.030
You like these, right?

00:14:55.470 --> 00:14:59.740
We may have dreamed, imagined, fantasized,

00:14:59.740 --> 00:15:03.230
and spent time in a world that wasn't real.

00:15:03.710 --> 00:15:08.970
But some of it was real, like this cat.

00:15:11.180 --> 00:15:15.050
You mean the feeling of 
truly loving something.

00:15:15.050 --> 00:15:15.730
Yeah.

00:15:15.730 --> 00:15:20.980
So it's okay to dream, 
imagine, and fantasize?

00:15:20.980 --> 00:15:22.440
I think so.

00:15:22.440 --> 00:15:25.390
If you don't dream, 
you'll never get anywhere.

00:15:25.390 --> 00:15:29.720
Creativity begins with imagining 
what you want to create.

00:15:34.750 --> 00:15:37.120
Misa-chan, are you sure?

00:15:37.120 --> 00:15:38.820
You can stay here.

00:15:38.820 --> 00:15:42.670
Then we could be creative together forever.

00:15:42.670 --> 00:15:45.930
There are lots of cute things here, indeed.

00:15:45.930 --> 00:15:50.420
It's because people like you
who love cute things

00:15:50.420 --> 00:15:54.050
are free to create the 
things they like, indeed.

00:15:55.540 --> 00:15:59.780
Harajuku is a wonderful place 
that accepts all those things.

00:15:59.780 --> 00:16:02.440
I love Harajuku, indeed.

00:16:02.440 --> 00:16:03.460
Then...

00:16:04.060 --> 00:16:06.230
You should stay here.

00:16:07.200 --> 00:16:10.750
I'm sad to leave you, indeed.

00:16:10.750 --> 00:16:17.540
But my dream now is to make my own 
planet as creative as Harajuku, indeed.

00:16:21.510 --> 00:16:24.470
In that case, we can't stop you.

00:16:24.470 --> 00:16:26.460
You're like us.

00:16:26.460 --> 00:16:28.590
You dream of being creative.

00:16:28.590 --> 00:16:34.030
I'm sad to see you go, but 
you'll always have our support.

00:16:34.920 --> 00:16:39.000
Y-You can count on me 
to look after Misa-sama.

00:16:39.000 --> 00:16:41.760
Wow, the shrimp's finally speaking again!

00:16:41.760 --> 00:16:43.940
Can we trust you?

00:16:43.940 --> 00:16:46.560
Ebifurya wanted creativity, too.

00:16:46.990 --> 00:16:51.530
That's why I want to teach him 
the joy of creation, indeed.

00:16:51.530 --> 00:16:54.400
Like you taught me.

00:16:54.400 --> 00:16:55.980
Misa-sama...

00:16:55.980 --> 00:16:58.340
Misa-sama! Squeeze!

00:16:58.340 --> 00:17:00.310
I can't breathe.

00:17:01.830 --> 00:17:04.410
Misa together, Misa together.

00:17:06.480 --> 00:17:08.960
Misa-chan, you're not alone.

00:17:08.960 --> 00:17:10.630
Indeed.

00:17:11.670 --> 00:17:15.360
I'm sorry for stealing all those things, indeed.

00:17:15.360 --> 00:17:17.890
Is there any way to restore them?

00:17:17.890 --> 00:17:20.010
I'm sorry.

00:17:20.010 --> 00:17:24.600
It would be impossible to restore everything.

00:17:24.910 --> 00:17:27.620
But I'd like to return what we can, indeed.

00:17:27.620 --> 00:17:30.320
I'll do what I can, yes.

00:17:30.320 --> 00:17:31.860
That would be best.

00:17:31.860 --> 00:17:34.140
There must be people 
suffering because of this.

00:17:34.140 --> 00:17:36.920
We'll rebuild what can't be returned.

00:17:36.920 --> 00:17:38.920
We're going to be busy!

00:17:41.850 --> 00:17:43.120
Thank you.

00:17:44.290 --> 00:17:46.580
I'm sorry, indeed!

00:17:50.660 --> 00:17:52.840
Give us a call once in a while.

00:17:52.840 --> 00:17:55.420
I'll be too worried about you to sleep.

00:17:57.420 --> 00:17:59.660
See you later, Misa-chan.

00:17:59.660 --> 00:18:01.450
Later, indeed.

00:18:01.450 --> 00:18:05.810
Someday we'll build a rocket and go see you.

00:18:05.810 --> 00:18:10.660
I'll become an internationally famous 
actress and make it to space, too.

00:18:10.660 --> 00:18:12.900
Roll out the red carpet for me.

00:18:14.420 --> 00:18:17.030
Let's create together again someday.

00:18:19.800 --> 00:18:26.470
I love this town, and I love you, indeed!

00:18:37.820 --> 00:18:39.360
They're gone.

00:18:39.920 --> 00:18:42.200
But I'm sure we'll see them again.

00:18:42.200 --> 00:18:43.560
I have a feeling we will.

00:18:43.560 --> 00:18:44.600
Yeah.

00:18:44.600 --> 00:18:48.010
With that UFO, I'm sure she 
can easily come and visit.

00:18:48.010 --> 00:18:48.780
Yeah.

00:18:51.780 --> 00:18:52.750
What?

00:18:52.750 --> 00:18:58.190
I should've asked for one of 
their ships so I could study it!

00:18:58.190 --> 00:19:00.630
Oh, that?

00:19:00.630 --> 00:19:03.480
Why don't you ask for one 
the next time they're here?

00:19:03.480 --> 00:19:05.800
Do you think I'll need a driver's license?

00:19:09.160 --> 00:19:12.010
Something's not right.

00:19:12.010 --> 00:19:13.220
Yeah.

00:19:14.000 --> 00:19:19.170
It looks like they returned a bunch of 
stuff, but they didn't get it right.

00:19:19.400 --> 00:19:21.840
But this is okay in its own way.

00:19:26.800 --> 00:19:29.260
So where should we start?

00:19:29.260 --> 00:19:30.780
Well, naturally...

00:19:30.780 --> 00:19:32.210
With Park?

00:19:32.210 --> 00:19:33.150
Yeah.

00:19:33.530 --> 00:19:34.600
What's that?

00:19:34.600 --> 00:19:35.610
Over there.

00:19:35.610 --> 00:19:36.710
There are people.

00:19:36.710 --> 00:19:37.790
Are they real?

00:19:37.790 --> 00:19:40.570
Maybe they came back since the bubble's gone.

00:19:41.300 --> 00:19:44.530
We aren't the only ones who love Harajuku.

00:19:44.930 --> 00:19:46.610
Good work, everyone.

00:19:46.610 --> 00:19:48.540
Come have some crêpes.

00:19:48.540 --> 00:19:49.600
This voice...

00:19:49.600 --> 00:19:52.170
Come on, everyone, get in line!

00:19:52.420 --> 00:19:54.370
S-Sayumin?

00:19:54.370 --> 00:19:56.540
But she seems a little different.

00:19:59.490 --> 00:20:00.260
Here.

00:20:00.880 --> 00:20:03.510
You girls can have some, too.

00:20:03.510 --> 00:20:04.720
Let's do our best.

00:20:05.330 --> 00:20:06.410
We will.

00:20:06.410 --> 00:20:07.430
Yeah.

00:20:08.800 --> 00:20:10.000
Thanks.

00:20:12.550 --> 00:20:13.780
Rito, how's the sign coming?

00:20:13.780 --> 00:20:14.920
Almost done.

00:20:14.920 --> 00:20:15.900
I'll help.

00:20:15.900 --> 00:20:17.110
Me, too!

00:20:17.540 --> 00:20:19.570
Notifications sent.

00:20:18.980 --> 00:20:19.560
<b>Notifications Sent</b>

00:20:21.420 --> 00:20:24.120
What? Did you remember a funny joke?

00:20:24.120 --> 00:20:27.660
No. I just realized I'm drawing a cat again.

00:20:28.010 --> 00:20:30.370
You sure do like cats.

00:20:30.370 --> 00:20:33.880
Yeah. The first time I drew a cat well,

00:20:33.880 --> 00:20:36.500
no one paid attention to it, 
but I was still happy.

00:20:36.820 --> 00:20:39.250
Maybe that's what I like.

00:20:40.240 --> 00:20:45.900
At first I just copied illustrations, 
but through imitating and copying,

00:20:45.900 --> 00:20:50.350
I started coming up with my own ideas and 
learned to create original drawings.

00:20:50.840 --> 00:20:54.060
It made me so happy, 
I haven't stopped drawing.

00:20:54.060 --> 00:20:57.420
I'm surprised. You started 
with copying, too.

00:20:58.090 --> 00:21:00.200
Trends are important,

00:21:00.200 --> 00:21:06.120
but I want to find what I really like
among them and create stuff!

00:21:06.120 --> 00:21:11.080
Yeah. Let's keep creating 
the things we like together.

00:21:13.210 --> 00:21:14.160
Yeah.

00:21:21.780 --> 00:21:22.840
It's done.

00:21:32.490 --> 00:21:34.760
Ready, prima donna?

00:21:34.760 --> 00:21:37.480
Of course. It's showtime!

00:21:37.690 --> 00:21:38.910
Open!

00:21:39.680 --> 00:21:41.900
Welcome!

00:21:42.680 --> 00:21:46.600
Today's dessert is coriander sweet potatoes.

00:21:46.600 --> 00:21:48.680
I bet that'll be popular!

00:21:48.680 --> 00:21:51.480
Rito, could you design the package?

00:23:25.960 --> 00:23:26.960
<b>Illustrated by Tamano Hazuki</b>

00:23:27.960 --> 00:23:28.970
<b>Illustrated by Ezaki Bisuko</b>

00:23:31.970 --> 00:23:32.970
<b>Illustrated by Chikuwa Mieru</b>

00:23:32.970 --> 00:23:33.970
<b>Illustrated by Kiato</b>

00:23:34.970 --> 00:23:35.970
<b>Illustrated by NC Teikoku</b>

00:23:35.970 --> 00:23:39.980
<b>Illustrated by Tanaka Mugi</b>
